{"ts": "2026-10-13T02:21:40+00:00", "run_id": "eval-E1-r2-20261013-002636", "server": "aflaguard", "tool": "draft_household_advisory", "inputs": {"household_id": "HH-004", "lot_id": "LOT-26-0004"}, "ms": 2, "output": {"draft_id": "ADV-0001", "status": "draft", "kind": "advisory", "household_id": "HH-004", "lot_id": "LOT-26-0004", "risk_level": "high", "sms_text": "Aflaguard: HH-004, lot LOT-26-0004 (8 bags). Do not sell or eat this lot until aflatoxin test results are back. Re-dry the maize on a tarp or raised rack until it is below 13.5% moisture. Rain fell while this maize was drying. Remove mouldy or discoloured grain. Dry maize on a tarp or raised rack, never on bare ground. Once dry, store in hermetic bags to stop mould growth. Start drying within 3 days of harvest. Safe limits: 13.5% moisture, 10 ppb total aflatoxin (EAS 2). - County Agriculture Office", "sources": ["CHIRPS:Makueni:2026-02-13..2026-02-23", "EAS 2 Maize grains - Specification", "households:HH-004", "lots:LOT-26-0004", "moisture_readings:MR-0010", "practice_survey:PS-004"], "next_step": "Call request_officer_approval with this draft_id. It cannot be sent until approved."}}
